# PART I — THE ULTIMATE MISSION

## 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Transform the entire MoonWitness repository into a modern, complete, extensible, enterprise-grade application platform inspired by Odoo, but engineered with more modern architecture, improved modularity, better developer experience, higher performance, cleaner abstractions, and stronger platform integration.

This is not a simple refactoring project.

This is not just a backend modernization.

This is not just a Next.js frontend implementation.

This is not just an ORM implementation.

This is a complete transformation of the engineering foundation, application runtime, module architecture, data system, user interface, and developer ecosystem.

The final platform must provide a unified architecture where:

- ORM defines data structures and business models.
- Addons define and extend platform capabilities.
- Model Registry manages model discovery and metadata.
- View Engine defines how models are presented.
- Action Engine defines how operations are executed.
- Security Engine controls access.
- API/RPC exposes consistent platform capabilities.
- Web Runtime renders dynamic applications.
- Shared Packages provide reusable infrastructure.
- Skin Engine controls visual presentation.
- Core Runtime coordinates the complete ecosystem.

All components must follow common contracts.

There must not be multiple independent systems solving the same problem.

**The objective is to build one platform, not a collection of loosely connected applications.**

## 2. TARGET PRODUCT

MoonWitness must become a complete application platform with the capabilities of a modular ERP framework and a modern application runtime.

It should be:

1. ORM-first.
2. Addon-native.
3. Model–View-driven.
4. Metadata-driven.
5. API/RPC-consistent.
6. Permission-aware.
7. Highly extensible.
8. Reusable across applications.
9. Configurable through addons.
10. Themeable through a centralized skin system.
11. Lightweight in execution.
12. Maintainable in architecture.
13. Secure by default.
14. Production-ready.
15. Developer-friendly.

Take inspiration from Odoo's strongest architectural concepts, but do not blindly reproduce its historical implementation, technical limitations, legacy patterns, or unnecessary complexity.

Use contemporary engineering practices and retain the strongest aspects of the existing MoonWitness technology stack.

## 3. PRIMARY RULE

**DO NOT STOP AT ANALYSIS. IMPLEMENT THE TRANSFORMATION.**

Work through:

DISCOVER → AUDIT → BRAINSTORM → DESIGN → PRIORITIZE → IMPLEMENT → INTEGRATE → TEST → OPTIMIZE → VERIFY.

Do not spend the entire execution session creating roadmaps, architecture diagrams, GitHub issues, or documentation.

Every useful finding should lead to an engineering decision and, whenever safely possible, an actual code change.

